Comments are appreciated on the following:

What I propose is a solution to game balance/design issues with Scroll
of Genocide. Currently monsters cannot use them which is an extreme
bias towards the player.

Playability problems arise with monsters being able to use ?oGen as
they could just Genocide you and end the game (insta-death). Since
sleeping monsters could be generated with them and read them on waking
it's very scary indeed.

So, in order to provide better storyline continuity, to enhance game
play, and to equalize game balance, I propose the following:

1) Add to the game a non-wishable Artifact lenses (Spectacles of the
Third Dimension or some such name).
2) Make scrolls of genocide only result in confusion when read without
said Artifact lenses.
3) Add a new dungeon branch (perhaps with an elven theme with trees,
forest type monsters, streams and such).
4) On the final level generate a peaceful nemesis with the Artifact
lenses being worn, and a pocket full of random scrolls (and a few ?oGen
besides).
5) Let monsters read scroll of genocide on low hp, targeting a hostile
creature (player included) if they have the Artifact lenses worn.

This makes it an optional quest with high risk in order to be able to
use this extremely biased spell.
The player would have to defeat a peaceful monster that could easily
Genocide *Him*. In order to get around this the player would have to be
creative in the use of pets as Genocide fodder or have some kind of
1-hit kill at his disposal or something.
The risks of bringing the lenses into the game is that any intelligent
monster could somehow acquire them and use a scroll on the player
(Rodney for example might steal them).

Think about it...

